//! Red-team battery against the Candidate B full-VU prover (`verity-direct` `ChainAir`, PROTOCOL.md 12).
//!
//! Every case is an *adversarial trace* (not an honest negative): rows are regenerated by the lane's own witness
//! generator with the forger's values imposed (`IntCtx::overrides`), so every downstream hint is honest for the
//! forged value and only the chain / boundary machinery can catch it.  Each case is run through (a) the lane's
//! concrete constraint evaluator (`air::chain_failing_rows`: which named constraints fail, if any) and (b) the real
//! Plonky3 prover + verifier at the lane's `DEFAULT_FRI` parameters, over Goldilocks and BabyBear.  A case the
//! verifier ACCEPTS while `expected = reject` is a forgery (status `FORGED`).
//!
//!   redteam-vu-b battery --root fixtures/bench-instances/v1 --out DIR [--field goldilocks|babybear|both] [--queries Q]
//!   redteam-vu-b challenger --out DIR [--samples 100000]
//!
//! Build in release: in a debug build uni-stark's prover asserts every constraint and panics on a forged trace
//! before any proof exists (that is not the verifier's verdict).

